## Side-Effect Policy

Inspect first and summarize intended changes before applying requested edits.
An explicit request authorizes necessary reversible local edits within its scope;
reuse applicable approval. Destructive actions, external sends, protected-input
access, and live/device actions require explicit authority. Preserve original
sources, unrelated user changes, and private data. Add project-specific limits here.

## Verification Plan

Check the requested content or changed behavior and every requirement of this
project's applicable policy. Run required integration checks for shared changes.
Report selected checks not run as NOT RUN with a reason; do not invent tests to
complete a form. Define project-specific commands and acceptance conditions here.

## Closeout Receipt

Report the requested result, relevant changes, checks and their scope, and any
remaining decisions or risks. State the next action only when one is needed.
Create a separate receipt file only when the task or project policy requires it.
